Part 2 - Enterprise Decision Making

## Scenario 1

Recommended Object:
View

Reasoning:
A View can display only Employee Name and Department Name while hiding sensitive information such as salary.
This provides controlled access and improves data security without exposing the underlying tables.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

## Scenario 2

Recommended Object:
Trigger

Reasoning:
A Trigger can automatically execute whenever a salary update occurs.
It is commonly used for auditing because it records changes immediately without requiring manual intervention from users or applications.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

## Scenario 3

Recommended Object:
Scheduler Job

Reasoning:
A Scheduler Job can automatically run at a specific date and time.
It is ideal for generating reports every Friday at 4:00 PM without requiring manual execution by users.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

## Scenario 4

Recommended Object:
Procedure

Reasoning:
A Procedure provides a reusable process that can calculate annual bonuses whenever needed.
It centralizes the business logic in one place, making maintenance and updates easier.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

## Scenario 5

Recommended Object:
Trigger

Reasoning:
A Trigger can automatically execute whenever an employee's salary is modified.
It can generate notifications or record events immediately after the salary update occurs.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

## Scenario 6

Recommended Object:
View

Reasoning:
A View provides a secure and simplified way to display employee information for dashboards.
Users can access the required data without direct access to the underlying tables, improving security and data control.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------